From e203e617974371c14f5aaa8b36bfa4c1794bb8e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 07:44:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: run the TypeScript job on Node 20, 22 and 24

The build-and-test matrix pinned 24 alone. That is what let the package's
declared engines floor drift away from the tested one unnoticed: `engines`
said 24 for no reason anyone could point at, and nothing in CI would have
noticed had it said 20 all along.

It now spans the supported range, so the floor the package declares is the
floor CI proves. Node 20 is the floor because a negated character class under
the `u` flag does not match an astral character before V8 11, which breaks
TypeScript-to-port regexp parity on Node 18.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LN5qWCMeZPzvMqXsj1Veoi
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 2e908bb..a388d84 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ jobs:
       fail-fast: false
       matrix:
         os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest, macos-latest]
-        node-version: [24.x]
+        node-version: [20.x, 22.x, 24.x]
 
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
 
-- 
